 "why_this_is_not_merely_untidy": "An Anukramani names a per-verse metre precisely when it differs from the hymn's. So the disagreement is the index working, and the defect is that the inherited edge was not withdrawn when the explicit one arrived. A consumer reading HAS_CHANDAS on AVS 6.73.1 is handed both bhurij and traistubham at identical confidence, with quality_tier as the only thing that could break the tie -- and nothing in the API contract says a reader must.",
